V41 (AP side of the encoder: venc_vcu_if.c + venc_common_if.c + enc_pm + intr as a host library, plus the n2vc_dma_* mirror) starting. Read PLAN/TASK/WORKER_RULES/FACTS 5-6, n2vc_hw.h, venc_ipi_msg.h, venc_vcu_if.c, venc_common_if.c, mtk_vcu.c. Host-only; no phone.

On the real phone the AP is NOT a /dev/vcu client: the kernel V4L2 driver is. mtk_vcu.c has two directions:
 (a) AP(kernel) -> VCU(daemon): vcu_ipi_send() (mtk_vcu.c:383-476) fills vcu->user_obj[i] {id,len,buf}, sets ipi_got[i], and the DAEMON pulls it with VCU_GET_OBJECT (vcu_ipi_get, :478-530, which also sets ipi_done[i] on entry); the AP waits for ipi_id_ack[id] (set by the daemon VCU_SET_OBJECT -> vcu_ipi_handler, :1396) and then for ipi_done[i].
 (b) VCU(daemon) -> AP: daemon ioctl VCU_SET_OBJECT; vcu_ipi_handler() dispatches to the registered handler for that id (vcu_enc_ipi_handler in venc_vcu_if.c:68) and wakes ack_wq.
So my AP library needs the kernel role, not the ioctl role. Please expose in vcu/n2vcu.h (names negotiable, semantics not):

  typedef int (*n2vcu_ipi_handler_t)(void *priv, void *data, unsigned len);

  /* vcu_ipi_register(): one handler per ipi id; returns 0 or -errno */
  int n2vcu_ap_register(struct n2vcu *v, unsigned ipi_id, n2vcu_ipi_handler_t h, void *priv);

  /* vcu_ipi_send(): queue {id,len,msg} for the daemon GET_OBJECT at ipi slot
     ipi_id_to_inst_id(id), then wait until (1) a VCU_IPIMSG for this id has
     been dispatched to my registered handler (ack) and (2) the daemon has
     come back for the next message (done). Returns 0, -EPERM if server not
     running, -EIO on abort, -ETIMEDOUT after timeout_ms. */
  int n2vcu_ap_send(struct n2vcu *v, unsigned ipi_id, const void *msg, unsigned len, void *priv, unsigned timeout_ms);

  /* vcu_mapping_dm_addr(): VCU DMEM address (the vcu_inst_addr in INIT_DONE,
     and the vsi pointer the AP reads/writes) -> AP-readable host pointer, or
     NULL if 0/out of range. In our model DMEM is guest memory. */
  void *n2vcu_dm_addr(struct n2vcu *v, uint32_t addr);
  /* optional but useful for bounds: 0 or byte length of the DMEM window */
  uint32_t n2vcu_dm_len(struct n2vcu *v);

  int n2vcu_open(struct n2vcu *v, struct n2vc_hw *hw, ...);  /* your existing constructor, I do not care about its args */
  void n2vcu_close(struct n2vcu *v);

If you prefer an opaque handle type (struct n2vcu_ap *) or a different constructor name, say so and give me the exact prototypes; I will code to them and my test_v41 will provide the same prototypes as a stand-in until your file lands. Two questions: (1) does your model serialize per IPI id like vcu_mutex[i]/user_obj[i] (16 slots, VCU_CODEC_MAX), i.e. one outstanding AP message per id? (2) is the DMEM window one guest allocation whose base you can give me (vcu_dm_addr(addr) is enough - I will not poke inside it except through that pointer)? I need no mmap and no GCE from you for V41.
